sequenceDiagram
    participant SP as Startup process
    participant WR as walreceiver
    participant SHM as WalRcvData (shmem)
    participant PM as Postmaster
    participant PRI as Primary walsender

    Note over SP: WaitForWALToBecomeAvailable<br/>decides XLOG_FROM_STREAM
    SP->>SHM: lock; receiveStart=LSN;<br/>receiveStartTLI=TLI;<br/>conninfo=...; slotname=...;<br/>walRcvState=STARTING; unlock
    SP->>PM: SendPostmasterSignal(PMSIGNAL_START_WALRECEIVER)
    PM->>WR: fork+exec WalReceiverMain
    WR->>WR: load_file libpqwalreceiver
    WR->>SHM: read receiveStart, conninfo
    WR->>PRI: walrcv_connect(conninfo)
    WR->>PRI: walrcv_identify_system
    PRI-->>WR: system_identifier, current TLI
    WR->>PRI: walrcv_startstreaming(receiveStart, slot)
    SP->>SP: WaitLatch(&WalRcv->latch,<br/>WL_LATCH_SET|WL_TIMEOUT,<br/>wal_retrieve_retry_interval)

    loop receive bytes
        PRI-->>WR: 'w' WAL bytes
        WR->>WR: XLogWalRcvWrite (pg_wal/seg)
        WR->>WR: XLogWalRcvFlush (fsync)
        WR->>SHM: writtenUpto/flushedUpto advance
        WR->>SP: SetLatch(&WalRcv->latch)
        SP->>SHM: GetWalRcvFlushRecPtr
        SHM-->>SP: flushedUpto = NEW_LSN
        SP->>SP: NEW_LSN >= RecPtr? yes
        SP->>SP: continue redo (read pg_wal segment)
    end

    Note over SP: at promotion or shutdown
    SP->>SHM: ShutdownWalRcv (set walRcvState=STOPPING)
    SP->>WR: WalRcvForceReply force_reply=1<br/>(optional final reply)
    WR->>PRI: walrcv_endstreaming + walrcv_disconnect
    WR->>WR: proc_exit(0)
